            <ArticleTitle>Refining the use of inhaled steroids in asthma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>558-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Inhaled corticosteroids remain the most significant aspect of asthma therapy. An increasing number of drugs, devices and formulations are available to health-care professionals. This article aims to address the goals of inhaled steroid therapy and asks how well the available options meet these goals.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
